     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I have a Shiny app that works locally, but gets this error when I try to deploy it to Shinyapps.io.<div><br></div><div><div style=\"border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(68,255,68);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,Courier,monospace;font-size:medium;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]](</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cond</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">object</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;draft.picks&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">not</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> found<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Calls</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">local</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tryCatch </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tryCatchList </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tryCatchOne </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Anonymous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Execution</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> halted</span></span></div></code></div><br><br></div><div>&quot;draft.picks&quot; is a locally stored data frame, which is used to create a reactive data frame that is used throughout the app. However, it is also used from the local data frame as well (to populate &quot;select&quot; objects on some filters that I didn&#39;t want to be affected by other reactive filters that might be in use). Does anybody have any idea how to troubleshoot this? Thanks.</div></div>"
